  "observations": [
    "The r_DisplayInfo debug overlay is on in every capture; its lower lines run across the shop panel's header and tab row, but no card.",
    "The location field reads SELECT LOCATION, so this entry has no location text: the terminal must come from the assortment check or the user (R-OCR-8).",
    "The buy cards show no AVAILABLE CARGO SIZE row at this terminal; Ruin Station's buy cards do.",
    "The sell tab is labelled 'Local Market Value'. Above IN DEMAND it shows a collapsed SELLABLE CARGO header, and a collapsed NO DEMAND header follows the last IN DEMAND card inside the shop panel (A21).",
    "Silicon is listed under IN DEMAND with 1,744 SCU and the status 'Out of Stock'; such cards are why the screen rule 'Out of Stock => 0 SCU' was dropped (O-131).",
    "Recycled Material Composite: the right-aligned '0 SCU' overlaps the end of the name (F6) in sell-1 and sell-2.",
    "Every sell capture scrolls by less than one page: the last card of one capture is partial and complete in the next, so consecutive captures overlap by about one card.",
    "The order of the IN DEMAND cards is not alphabetical by displayed name.",
    "Two prices differ from UEX's latest values recorded on 2026-10-10 (Laranite 8,700 against 8,200; DynaFlex 1,468 against 1,460); both were rechecked at 4x zoom.",
    "The [!] prefix of SLAM, Neon, E'tam, Revenant Tree Pollen and Altruciatoxin is part of the game's display name (global.ini wraps it in an <EM3> tag).",
    "Captured with the game's screenshot key while Windows HDR and the game's HDR were on (stated by the project owner). The files are 8-bit baseline JPEGs without an ICC profile, so the game tone-maps the HDR frame to SDR when it saves; how it does that is unmeasured (A16), and transfer stays null."
  ]
}
